<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rafael Trujillo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1891">1891</a>–<a href="/years/1961">1961</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rafael Trujillo was dictator of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a> from 1930 to 1961. He rose through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-guard-dominican-republic">National Guard</a> created during the US occupation and seized power in 1930. His rule combined a personality cult, terror and personal control of the economy, and in 1937 his troops massacred thousands of Haitians. He was assassinated in 1961.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rafael-trujillo.jpg" alt="Rafael Trujillo" width="320" height="455" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rafael_L._Trujillo_en_la_silla_presidencial_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1937 Dominican troops under <b>Rafael Trujillo</b> killed 20,000–30,000 Haitians on the border in the Parsley Massacre.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-haiti">Republic of Haiti · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Joaquín Balaguer, a former aide of <b>Trujillo</b>, defeated Juan Bosch and introduced a new constitution in November 1966.</blockquote><a href="/state/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a></li><li><blockquote>A new National Guard was trained, in which <b>Rafael Trujillo</b> rose quickly.</blockquote><a href="/state/military-government-of-santo-domingo">Military Government of Santo Domingo</a></li><li><blockquote>His attempt to extend his term weakened his government, and in 1930 <b>Rafael Trujillo</b>, commander of the US-trained army, took power in a coup and won a fraudulent election.</blockquote><a href="/state/third-dominican-republic">Third Dominican Republic</a></li></ul></section>
